{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Release critique lens A (correctness and refusal safety) for the pending 8.9.5 patch","packet_sha256":"dc178cf66cdd3ca602c9edc736b1f795f4e14412b1a4f22e08cb1fb00f6e0dca","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"294d9fb8d4ed1d5c262526b0fcf87ac48445f5b4ec54c87f4237f741e3e2abd7","verdict":"block","target_observations":[{"target":"task-run-persist-scope","verdict":"block","summary":"Normal classified candidates are narrowed, but malformed or incomplete candidate classification falls back to stage-everything and can carry out-of-scope residue.","evidence":["scripts/task_run/task_run_lane_runner.py: _in_scope_candidate_paths returns None whenever candidate.changed_paths is not a list.","scripts/task_run/task_run_lane_runner.py: persist_incomplete_candidate passes paths=None through to _commit_lane_snapshot.","scripts/task_run/task_run_git.py: _commit_lane_snapshot interprets paths=None as git add --all -- ., preserving the historical unscoped behavior.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_completion.py covers admitted, all-disallowed, and empty-list cases, but not a useful candidate with absent or malformed changed_paths."]},{"target":"release-resume-notes-placeholder","verdict":"pass","summary":"The resume planner distinguishes zero, one, and multiple drafted-notes candidates without silently selecting an ambiguous file.","evidence":["skills/public/release/scripts/plan_release_run_packets.py emits no --notes-file for zero candidates, the exact path for one candidate, and <notes-file> for multiple candidates.","tests/quality_gates/test_release_run_planner_prepared_stop.py verifies ambiguous, single, and absent notes-candidate behavior."]},{"target":"staged-eviction-owner","verdict":"block","summary":"The pre-commit owner selects staged test path names but analyzes working-tree bytes, allowing staged unsafe content to evade the gate when the same path is subsequently cleaned in the worktree.","evidence":["scripts/hooks/check_staged_cheap_owners.py obtains staged scope paths, then passes repo-relative path names to the eviction gate.","scripts/gates/check_module_eviction_form.py select_targets builds its universe from current filesystem paths and measure reads each selected path with path.read_text().","No reviewed code reads the staged blob with git show :path or otherwise verifies that index and worktree content match.","tests/quality_gates/test_module_eviction_form_gate.py changes and checks working-tree files directly; it does not exercise a staged-unsafe/worktree-clean split."]},{"target":"worker-expected-targets","verdict":"pass","summary":"Expected targets are propagated to finalization, where omission makes the worker report ineligible.","evidence":["skills/shared/scripts/reviewer_worker_runner_support.py declares repeatable --expected-target.","skills/shared/scripts/run_reviewer_worker.py passes args.expected_target to finalize_attempt.","tests/quality_gates/test_reviewer_runner.py verifies omission refusal, observed-target success, and unchanged target-free behavior."]},{"target":"prepared-target-worker-wiring","verdict":"pass","summary":"Live review execution validates the declaration's basic shape and passes every declared target into the file-backed worker invocation.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_execution.py refuses a non-list or any non-string, blank prepared target before constructing the live runner command.","skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_invocation.py emits one --expected-target argument per prepared target.","tests/quality_gates/test_review_target_coverage_floor.py exercises the end-to-end refusal and success paths."]},{"target":"lane-target-declaration","verdict":"pass","summary":"The generated reviewer prompt explicitly names declared targets and requires exactly one substantive observation for each.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_packet.py renders the prepared_targets list and requires exactly one target_observations entry per target with nonempty summary and evidence.","skills/public/critique/references/prepare-packet.md documents mirroring prepared targets into worker --expected-target declarations.","tests/quality_gates/test_review_target_coverage_floor.py verifies the dry-run prompt contains the target and exact-one instruction."]}],"findings":[{"id":"RC-A-001","severity":"high","summary":"The staged module-eviction gate can approve different bytes from those being committed.","evidence":["The hook derives names from the staged scope, but check_module_eviction_form.py reads selected paths from the working tree.","A developer can stage a test containing a forbidden sys.modules eviction, replace the working-tree version with clean content, and have the gate inspect the clean version while Git commits the unsafe staged blob.","The supplied tests do not cover index/worktree divergence."],"action":"Make the staged owner analyze index blobs, or fail closed whenever a selected staged path differs between index and worktree; add a regression test with unsafe staged bytes and clean working-tree bytes."},{"id":"RC-A-002","severity":"high","summary":"Completed-lane persistence retains an unscoped stage-all fallback when candidate scope metadata is missing or malformed.","evidence":["_in_scope_candidate_paths returns None for non-list changed_paths.","persist_incomplete_candidate treats None as legacy unclassified behavior.","_commit_lane_snapshot stages every path when paths is None, so useful malformed candidates can commit out-of-scope residue instead of refusing.","The new tests cover valid lists but not missing, tuple, string, or otherwise malformed classification."],"action":"For the completed-lane persistence caller, require a well-formed explicit admitted path list and refuse malformed or absent classification. Keep stage-all only behind a separately explicit legacy API if still required, and add malformed-classification regression tests."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Path-scoped eviction runs accept an empty intersection.","bin":"not-a-blocker","disposition":"This is appropriate for a precise staged selection outside the eviction universe; the broad whole-repo mode still refuses an empty universe."},{"concern":"Prepared-target validation does not run on dry-run.","bin":"follow-up","disposition":"Live execution refuses malformed basic declarations before worker launch. Tightening preview parity and duplicate/canonical-string validation would improve ergonomics, but the reviewed live approval path is not bypassed by this alone."},{"concern":"Resume notes omission when no drafted candidate is found.","bin":"not-a-blocker","disposition":"The reviewed contract intentionally omits --notes-file when discovery returns no candidate and explicitly exposes ambiguity with a placeholder when candidates exist."}],"next_move":"Block 8.9.5 until staged eviction checks judge index content and completed-lane persistence fails closed on absent or malformed scope classification; add adversarial regression tests for both escapes, then rerun the bounded release critique.","non_claims":["No workspace files were edited or commands executed.","This review judges only the identity-bound inline semantic payload, not current workspace state.","Passing observations for other targets do not offset the two release-blocking refusal-safety escapes.","Goal evidence was not bound to a Goal Run Work Item."]}
